implementationPlan.description:
THE NON-NESTING HAND-OVER in scripts/moe-agent.ps1.

1. Immediately after the param() block, before $ErrorActionPreference, add an in-process supervisor. Its comment must carry the why: df42861 kept the console but nested one blocked parent per reload (45 wrappers / 5.5 GB measured 2026-09-19); `&` on the script path re-reads the file, so each pass runs the bytes on disk now, and the previous pass has fully returned.

     if (-not $global:MoeWrapperSupervised) {
         $global:MoeWrapperSupervised = $true
         try {
             do {
                 $global:MoeWrapperReload = $false; $global:LASTEXITCODE = 0
                 & $PSCommandPath @PSBoundParameters
                 $moeRc = $LASTEXITCODE
             } while ($global:MoeWrapperReload)
         } catch {
             Write-Host "wrapper relaunch failed; the seat is stopped, relaunch it by hand: $_" -ForegroundColor Yellow
             $moeRc = 1
         } finally { $global:MoeWrapperSupervised = $false }
         exit $moeRc
     }

2. Every existing `exit N` in the body now returns N to this loop, which exits with it. The -Loop -NoLoop exit 2 and single-shot exits keep their codes. Ctrl+C stops the whole pipeline, so it never reloads.
3. Replace the bottom-of-file hand-over (`& $moeRelaunchExe @moeRelaunchArgs; exit $LASTEXITCODE`) with `$global:MoeWrapperReload = $true; exit 0`. Keep the in-loop hash check, the deregister 'wrapper_restart' and the break exactly as they are.
4. Delete $script:MoeWrapperHostExe and $script:MoeWrapperRelaunchArgs and their capture. Nothing else reads them; grep to confirm.
5. Rewrite the hand-over comment block: one process and one console per seat, however many reloads.
6. A side effect worth one sentence in that comment: the runner identity (<pid>@<start token>) now survives a reload, because the process is the same, so a held attempt can still reattach after a reload.

Error handling: a reload whose new parameter list rejects the old bound parameters, or whose file vanished, throws inside `&`. The supervisor's catch prints the same 'relaunch it by hand' line as today and exits 1 — the same outcome as today's failed child relaunch.
